Use `embedMany` to embed multiple chunks in a single call, and implement your own concurrency control to limit how many requests run at once.

```ts
import { embedMany } from 'ai';

async function embedChunksInBatches(
  allChunks: string[],
  batchSize: number,
  maxConcurrent: number,
) {
  // Simple concurrency limiter
  const results: Array<{ embedding: number[]; content: string }> = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < allChunks.length; i += batchSize) {
    const batch = allChunks.slice(i, i + batchSize);
    const { embeddings } = await embedMany({
      model: 'openai/text-embedding-3-small',
      values: batch,
    });
    results.push(...embeddings.map((e, idx) => ({ content: batch[idx], embedding: e })));
  }
  return results;
}
```

`embedMany` handles splitting large payloads automatically [7], so you only need to manage batch size and concurrency yourself.

